# A geometric loop.  The block comment below holds text that is not a program; the reader must skip
# it whole.  A block comment opens with the two characters hash and equals, and a line comment that
# also matched them used to win, so the block's body was parsed and refused as a syntax error.
# Expected: the tool answers unknown (it gives no bound for this query), not a syntax error.
Y := 0;
while flip(1/2) {
    Y += 1;
}
return Y

#= Original code:

while ( x > 0 ) {
    {x := x + 1} [ 1/2 ] {x := x - 1};
}

=#
